{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan","id":1389560,"title":"Pick your clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-17T21:28:31-07:00","id":1389560,"title":"Pick your clan","content":"Let's say some magical being popped up one day and decided to make you choose to be a VTM 5th edition 8th gen vampire. If you don't pick one, the magical being will just pick one at random for you. You have your real life attributes and skills, and five in each of your clan Disciplines. You can pick the power you get for each Discipline level. You can never learn out of clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Caitiff is not an option. Must be a clan that has been detailed in 5th edition.<br /> <br /> There are no other magical beings in the world, unless you decide to embrace at some point. Even the creature you transformed you is from another dimension, and he leaves this universe laughing after turning you.<br /> <br /> Which clan do you pick?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T21:31:32-07:00","id":1389561,"title":"","content":"Either Tremere or Malkavian. Do I get to learn rituals too? If not, Malkavian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T21:57:18-07:00","id":1389564,"title":"","content":"Malkavian.<br /> <br /> I'm already crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T22:02:03-07:00","id":1389565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoktorNiemand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389561#post1389561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either Tremere or Malkavian. Do I get to learn rituals too? If not, Malkavian.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can sacrifice points in your disciplines for the equivalent experience worth of rituals. In other words you could, for example, drop your Dominate down to 4 for 25 XP worth of rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T01:52:36-07:00","id":1389594,"title":"","content":"Do I get to pick my Ventrue feeding type?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, Toreador. It's the most applicable to the modern world given the state so far of Thaumaturgy in V5. Auspex might've gotten nerfed to the ground, but Presence is amazing and super useful. The most important thing is that the weakness is weak (unless it changed?) otherwise I'd have picked malkavian (and subsequently saved the world). It's all about standard of living and not getting caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T02:11:39-07:00","id":1389598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389594#post1389594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I get to pick my Ventrue feeding type?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, Toreador. It's the most applicable to the modern world given the state so far of Thaumaturgy in V5. Auspex might've gotten nerfed to the ground, but Presence is amazing and super useful. The most important thing is that the weakness is weak (unless it changed?) otherwise I'd have picked malkavian (and subsequently saved the world). It's all about standard of living and not getting caught.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that feeding type must be, at most, ten percent of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T02:53:35-07:00","id":1389603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan#post1389560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say some magical being popped up one day and decided to make you choose to be a VTM 5th edition 8th gen vampire. If you don't pick one, the magical being will just pick one at random for you. You have your real life attributes and skills, and five in each of your clan Disciplines. You can pick the power you get for each Discipline level. You can never learn out of clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Caitiff is not an option. Must be a clan that has been detailed in 5th edition.<br /> <br /> There are no other magical beings in the world, unless you decide to embrace at some point. Even the creature you transformed you is from another dimension, and he leaves this universe laughing after turning you.<br /> <br /> Which clan do you pick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, I'd tell him to screw off and come back when he could make me a V20 5th gen. Now THAT would be a real offer!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But, in all seriousness, I'd probably go with Toreador. Sexy, persuasive, rich and with no major weakness outside of what vampires get by default. Not to mention having the ability to read peoples minds and run faster than Speedy friggin Gonzalez.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T05:01:09-07:00","id":1389635,"title":"","content":"Lasombra...or Brujah, their lore kinda sucks tho<br /> <br /> I would pick Toreador, but their clan features (bane/compulsions) need to be more specific<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T05:10:01-07:00","id":1389638,"title":"","content":"I'd pick the Brujah. Fits my RL politics, my life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T06:04:58-07:00","id":1389646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruthven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389638#post1389638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd pick the Brujah. Fits my RL politics, my life.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Brujah all over the political spectrum, how can that fit anybody?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T06:17:14-07:00","id":1389647,"title":"","content":"Tremere or Ministry, but if I didn't need to worry about the bane, Malkavian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 05-18-2020, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T06:21:29-07:00","id":1389649,"title":"","content":"As it's V5 and Ravnos isn't an option, I'd go for Ventrue. Fortitude's redesign has given it a lot of neat survivability options and supernatural stoicism. Pair that with Auspex as an Antitribu (if they ever get printed) and you can just win at cards every time you play. I'm sure there's other benefits to being able to read minds, but they elude me. Otherwise, Presence at 5 is just busted. Everyone goes for Majesty but being able to Awe / Daunt / Entrance through live feeds where Dominate cannot work (even with Irresistible Voice) is insanely good when used right.<br /> <br /> Oh, and having Dominate with Rationalize seems like an easy way to never want for anything, either. Just gotta pray you don't end up with a feeding type of &quot;women born in 1972 with an addiction to opiates and a foot fetish&quot; or something similarly vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26082-mulengro","name":"Mulengro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T06:24:57-07:00","id":1389650,"title":"","content":"Gangrel. There's nothing more to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T06:29:13-07:00","id":1389651,"title":"","content":"Okay, let\u2019s do it the other way around.<br /> <br /> If there are no other supernatural beings, Hecata are pretty pointless.<br /> <br /> I would also avoid every clan with Auspex, I think you would become crazy, if you are not already (I looking at you malk!) if you would have to deal with the knowledge, Auspex provides you with. If not the pure information, the philosophical implications would screw you up. Therefor no Toreador, no Malkavian and no Tremere for me (while Tremere and the rituals would be a nice way to get some more stuff to do and if there is no other vampire, their bane would become pretty much nonexistent. Okay maybe Tremere...).<br /> <br /> Banu Haquim are interesting for blood sorcery, but I can\u2019t see me in the narrow mindset of \u201cfollow the rules\u201d!<br /> <br /> Lasombra are kind of cool, but if their oblivion works or not with the \u201cno supernatural creature\u201d restriction might be arguable. And I would be pissed if I would loose my ability to use electronics.<br /> <br /> Brujah are pretty much pointless in that scenario. Irl you don\u2019t have to fight as often, so Potence and celerity are not on my priority list. And the Higher risk of Rage seams a huge risk of screwing your own or someone else life. No Brujah for my, thanks!<br /> <br /> Nosferatu... would I lost my beauty? Probably not much, but still, I am a social person, that seams to risky for my.<br /> <br /> If I don\u2019t miss anything we are left with Ventrue, Gangrel and Ministry.<br /> <br /> Gangrel would be nice for Animalism and Fortitude. Both would help you to counter the worst aspects of being a Vampire. The new Bane is not to bad either. Pretty good.<br /> <br /> Ventrue have fortitude too. And they have Presence and Dominate, great for getting blood relatively easy. It would depend on your feeding restriction. A to narrow feeding restriction could end up in having a hard time to slack your hunger.<br /> <br /> The Ministry don\u2019t have animalism or Fortitude, but obfuscate and Presence are great tools too. And Protean would be a great toy to play with. But the bane... it sounds nice and is definitely the kind of character I love play, but it is not necessarily the kind of character I want to be.<br /> <br /> So, I would be pleased with either of the three, but if I have to choose, I would pick the Gangrel... no wait, the Ventrue... no wait...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:42:39-07:00","id":1389667,"title":"","content":"Dunno. Do not have 5 but if Caitiff is not an option and I can not refure to being not Vampire most likely Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T08:24:29-07:00","id":1389671,"title":"","content":"I'd go for Ministry. Turning into mist, drifting into libraries and bookstores after closing, reading in the dark and if I would go and be with other folks, I have the choice to be entirely unnoticable or the most awesome person they have ever met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T08:53:48-07:00","id":1389675,"title":"","content":"Toreador. I\u2019m both an artist and a Beautiful Person (or at least a pretty person). I also like visual arts, music and good writing, so the Toreador flaw would definitely apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T09:21:45-07:00","id":1389679,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce please!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T09:34:53-07:00","id":1389680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389679#post1389679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tzimisce please!</div> </div> </div> </div>Be cautious what you wish for. We still don\u2019t know how they will turn out in V5, it might be a surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T12:08:13-07:00","id":1389719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389680#post1389680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be cautious what you wish for. We still don\u2019t know how they will turn out in V5, it might be a surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vicissitude is cool enough to be worth the risk. Admittedly it's possible Viscissitude could be altered significantly and it'll probably be rolled into Protean, but it's such a thematic and central power to the concept of the Tzimisce I can't see them getting rid of their flesh-warping powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-18-2020, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T13:00:59-07:00","id":1389735,"title":"","content":"Sethos, Yes, the Brujah cut across the political spectrum. I suppose I was inferring their significant role in the current Anarch Movement, which is anti-establishment. It's simplification, no doubt.. I suppose my simplification is, not every anarch is an anarchist, but every vampire anarchist is likely an anarch,a nd the Brujah would have their fair share of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:09:28-07:00","id":1389747,"title":"","content":"Gangrel. Alley cats already follow me, to the point that staff from neighboring restaurants call me the Cat Whisperer, my vet's grouchy parrot will talk to me while ignoring other people in the waiting room, and it's exceedingly rare for a dog to take a dislike to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:14:56-07:00","id":1389751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389719#post1389719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicissitude is cool enough to be worth the risk. Admittedly it's possible Viscissitude could be altered significantly and it'll probably be rolled into Protean, but it's such a thematic and central power to the concept of the Tzimisce I can't see them getting rid of their flesh-warping powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They will get a way to warp their flesh, at least some of them. But we don\u2019t know how that will work. We know about for sure, there will not be a Vicissitude discipline. After the Chicago Folios the speculation is, they will probably have Blood Sorcery (I can see BS Powers that allow you to alter your body). They might get protean as well, but if so, they will lose Auspex or Animalism and there are pretty good arguments for and against both.<br /> <br /> I think the Bane will be stay as we know it, but we have no clue how the Clan compulsion might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:16:17-07:00","id":1389752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruthven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389735#post1389735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sethos, Yes, the Brujah cut across the political spectrum. I suppose I was inferring their significant role in the current Anarch Movement, which is anti-establishment. It's simplification, no doubt.. I suppose my simplification is, not every anarch is an anarchist, but every vampire anarchist is likely an anarch,a nd the Brujah would have their fair share of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you are coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T17:47:33-07:00","id":1389797,"title":"","content":"Wait. By &quot;no other supernatural creatures&quot;, do you mean no other vampires? Ventrue looks less good if there's no social structure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T17:49:06-07:00","id":1389799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389797#post1389797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. By &quot;no other supernatural creatures&quot;, do you mean no other vampires? Ventrue looks less good if there's no social structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>None. Of course, there's nothing stopping you from popping out a bunch of baby 9th gens if that's your desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:34:23-07:00","id":1389968,"title":"","content":"Gangrel. I basically want to be the male version of Princess Mononoke.<br /> <br /> The clan flaw would suck but I think you'd get over it after a few hundred years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T08:23:44-07:00","id":1389982,"title":"","content":"I'm not especially familiar with V5, but I would probably choose Tremere, conditional on one question: before someone asked about rituals, and the idea was sacrificing dots of Blood Sorcery (that's the V5 term I believe?) for them, but would one be allowed to start with their 5 dots in Blood Sorcery, along with Auspex and Dominate, and then just make like the original Tremere did and start learning/designing rituals after &quot;character gen&quot;?<br /> <br /> Sure, it would take decades or centuries, but we've established a context where there is no other supernatural threat in existence and I am at the top of a currently-nonexistent Pyramid. Similarly, the Tremere weakness of V5, no blood-bonding other vampires, doesn't really hurt in a world where I am the first vampire and start with Dominate 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T09:35:38-07:00","id":1389989,"title":"","content":"Gangrel and a short unlife for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T10:21:44-07:00","id":1390000,"title":"","content":"I always say I\u2019d be Brujah, but if I\u2019m honest with myself, I might actually be Ministry. Great discipline spread there, clan bane not too bad.<br /> <br /> The reason I didn\u2019t go with Tremere is that they\u2019re really dependent on structure and each other. Otherwise, vampire wizard would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 05-19-2020, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T15:52:22-07:00","id":1390085,"title":"","content":"This is a big decision, right? Requires careful, overly analytical pondering. Shared with others via stream of consciousness rambling.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Disciplines</b></u><br /> (in order of preference)<br /> <br /> <u>Dominate</u> Several lower level powers need no roll against mortals. Vastly useful, especially since nobody (including the courts) believe in mind control.<br /> <u>Presence</u> Classic social power fantasy. Rich, famous, etc. Gotta have either this or Dominate. Is taking both over-specializing?<br /> <u>Obfuscate</u> Invisibility is a classic superpower. Broadly useful.<br /> <u>Blood Sorcery</u> Taste for Blood and Extinguish Vitae completely useless. Blood of Potency close to useless. The rest are for somebody living in a video game. The rituals, though... hmmm.<br /> <u>Auspex</u> Sense the Unseen is not great in a mundane world. Otherwise, useful. Possession is an amalgam with Dominate, hmmm.<br /> <u>Fortitude</u> Again, not much combat expected with peers. This power protects me against environmental damage and accident, which is the main danger. Resilience and Unswayable Mind really shine at upper levels.<br /> <u>Protean</u> Similar environmental resistance to Fortitude, plus some combat ability with claws. Avoids the shame of being a vampire who can't see in the dark. Don't really need the travel powers, since, you know, cars exist. Weirdly, it's either this or Fortitude. Not both.<br /> <u>Animalism</u> Two powers work on other supernaturals: Sense the Beast, and Quell the Beast. Animals exist, so good there. Though, how useful is this really?<br /> <u>Potence</u> Useful for combat, yeah. But, if no one else in the world can blood surge and so forth, how badly do I need it? Might be worth it for Lethal Body, which almost instakills mortals. Above that might be overkill.<br /> <u>Celerity</u> Useful for combat, yeah. But, guns and running away exist. Plus, if no one else in the world can blood surge and so forth, how badly do I need it?<br /> <u>Nihilistics</u> Ghosts don't exist. Does the void? Mediocre power set anyway.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Clans</b></u><br /> (in order of preference)<br /> <br /> <u>Ventrue</u> Funny, even without the cachet of being the highest of high clans, still a good package mechanically. Disciplines are very great, great, and not bad. Bane is light-weight. Heck, I'd probably stick to feeding from my favorites, anyway. We may have a winner?<br /> <u>Ministry</u> Disciplines might be best in the game. No existing vampires means no snake-motif stigma. Bane is potentially quite fatal, but it's not like &quot;a little sunburn&quot; is a good idea for any vampire. Besides, they can meld with dirt now, so that helps. This clan is why I can't slam-dunk into Ventrue. <u><br /> Malkavian</u> Good discipline spread, good amalgams, and lots of synergy. Bane is super-harsh in the fluff; rather tame mechanically. Not much worse than say epilepsy or not well-controlled diabetes. This might work.<br /> <u>Tremere</u> Disciplines quite good. Weakness is a minor inconvenience, though complicates having baby-vamps. If I embraced I would want to blood bond them without mercy. Still, pretty darned good.<br /> <u>Banu Haqim</u> Disciplines are useless/flashy speed force powers, nice invisibility, and awesome magic. Where are the socials? Weakness does not exist in a world without other vampires. Even with other vampires it's pretty mild, if you're a little careful. This has potential.<br /> <u>Gangrel</u> Disciplines are middling to poor. No socials. Weakness only crops up on occasion, and if I have just frenzied growing a tail is the least of my worries. Maybe.<br /> <u>Toreador</u> Disciplines acceptable. Being rich sounds like fun, except the bane doesn't make you rich. It just makes being poor suck harder. Meh.<br /> <u>Lasombra</u> Weakness makes modern life difficult. Disciplines include one great one, one poor one, and Nihilistics. Probably, no.<br /> <u>Brujah</u> Two fairly useless disciplines, and one great one. Weakness too intrusive and damaging when it happens. In real world, frenzy looks like major psychosis... like crazier than V5 Malks. Hard no.<br /> <u>Nosferatu</u> No. Just no.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Final Winner</u></b><br /> <br /> First, a word about the runners-up.<br /> <br /> If this included V20, I'd have chosen Baali. Cool powers, classic weakness. Demons don't exist. Team Baali!<br /> <br /> Though, if V20 bloodlines and clan variants are in the mix.... I gotta give some love to Tzimisce with Basarab family heritage. Dominate, Protean, Vicissitude. Garlic allergy. The classics always satisfy. Wash off the body glitter, sister-friend, that's what I call a vampire.<br /> <br /> Back to V5. Malkavian, malkavian, malkavian. If you say it three times it becomes true. So much fluff, so much baggage. Mechanics have been so blanded down. The big problem is the childer. I wouldn't want to embrace total strangers, but if a friend went shredder? No. Not Malkavian. Maybe? Please? No!<br /> <br /> So, is it Ministry or Ventrue? Ventrue or Ministry?<br /> <br /> I could go either way.<br /> <br /> Ministry's weakness... noontime kills you dead. Okay. But, the bright light thing. It's rough.<br /> <br /> Ventrue. Much more manageable weakness. Too many social disciplines. Though... Dominate is and has always been soooo overpowered. Where is the Protean or Obfuscate or even Auspex?<br /> <br /> I want Dominate.<br /> <br /> Wait. I know what to pick.<br /> <br /> Fuck it.<br /> <br /> Ministry.<br /> <br /> Predator type: Cleaver.<br /> <br /> Now give me my starter level of Dominate, please. I said <b>NOW.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T19:43:06-07:00","id":1390896,"title":"","content":"let me get unbondable and I'm good as almost any clan, probably wouldn't want nossie because I don't want to have to invest in obfuscate that early on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T20:22:57-07:00","id":1390906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1389564#post1389564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malkavian.<br /> <br /> I'm already crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> I've always been drawn to the clan in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T15:21:13-07:00","id":1391791,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can see myself as a V5-era Malkavian. I don\u2019t like it when they\u2019re played for comedy, but I can relate to being so sensitive that sometimes you just can\u2019t even.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea that the Toreador and Malkavians are close kin, each of which manifests this hypersensitivity differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T16:20:27-07:00","id":1391804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389560-pick-your-clan?p=1390896#post1390896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let me get unbondable and I'm good as almost any clan, probably wouldn't want nossie because I don't want to have to invest in obfuscate that early on</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to &quot;invest&quot;. Read the original post: you get your clans at 5, but can never develop any out of clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T19:01:04-07:00","id":1391830,"title":"","content":"Hecata, Cappadocian has always been my favorite. Since they don\u2019t have an official write-up yet, though, I\u2019d go with Lasombra. It would suck that I couldn\u2019t use electronics, but everything they stand for is pretty much me in a nut shell anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26172-twilightspire","name":"Twilightspire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}